// PARAM: --analysis sign
// The concrete results are fixed -- min(3, -5) is -5 and max(3, -5) is 3 --
// and sign_min/sign_max answer them exactly: a negative argument on either
// side pins the minimum negative, and symmetrically for the maximum.
//
// What loses it is the norm at the special call's operating kind. min and max
// return one of their operands, so the result is representable whenever the
// operands are, and both were evaluated at int32. A Sign value carries no
// kind, so nothing at the norm can use that: gamma of Negative is unbounded,
// its wraparound at int32 may be positive, and topping is the only sound
// answer. 01-min_max_interval.vimp is the same program where the domain does
// carry the bound.
void main() {
  int32 w, x, y, z;
  x := 3;
  y := -5;
  z := min(x, y);
  w := max(x, y);
  __voblint_check(z < 0); // UNKNOWN
  __voblint_check(0 < w)  // UNKNOWN
}
